  "explains": "outstanding_total in billing/services.py changes. Two modules import it and use it: billing/views.py (invoice_list calls it) and billing/api.py (the overdue action of InvoiceViewSet calls it). billing/reports.py imports the same module but only format_reference, so it is excluded by narrowing. The walk goes from each importer up to the route: invoice_list is mounted at ANY /billing/invoices as in dj01. In the viewset only the overdue action calls the helper, so the route reached is that action's (the router makes it from the @action(detail=False) method: GET /api/v1/invoices/overdue, under api/v1/ from config/urls.py, through include(router.urls) and the register line); the list and detail routes of the same viewset, and the void action, are not reached. The unit test imports billing.views, a caller, and is stated as a unit test. On the web, INVOICES_URL fits the list route and OVERDUE_URL, written over two lines, fits the overdue route exactly (the literal overdue is more specific than the detail route's parameter); both are called by InvoiceListPage, one screen, whose first chain goes through billing/views.py. The monthly report page is not reached: its route runs reports.monthly, which calls format_reference.",
